{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1788420340134,"sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","part":{"id":"prt_06628b9a20015hx7kXyYjF76ZS","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904","messageID":"msg_06628b77c001t86rJBh5awsj3T","sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":22964,"input":6536,"output":19,"reasoning":33,"cache":{"write":0,"read":16376}},"cost":0.000334744}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788420341659,"sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","part":{"id":"prt_06628bf96001TJPTr4gOzwDD9x","messageID":"msg_06628b9d6001TT7KbpN0Dt83dZ","sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","snapshot":"4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788420343953,"sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_773fbe458ef0419889523ed2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Output Refinement with BestOfN and Refine\n\nThis tutorial covers two powerful modules for improving LLM output quality through retry-based refinement: `BestOfN` and `Refine`.\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen working with language models, occasional failures or suboptimal outputs are common. The `BestOfN` and `Refine` modules help you handle these cases by:\n\n- Running your module multiple times with varying temperatures\n- Selecting the best result based on a reward function\n- Providing configurable error tolerance through `fail_count`\n\n## Choosing Between BestOfN and Refine\n\n| Feature | BestOfN | Refine |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| Simple retry with selection | ✓ | ✓ |\n| Temperature variation | ✓ | ✓ |\n| Adaptive feedback from failures | ✗ | ✓ |\n| Module blame analysis | ✗ | ✓ |\n\n- **Use `BestOfN`** when you want simple retry-with-selection without feedback\n- **Use `Refine`** when you want adaptive feedback to improve subsequent attempts\n\n## Setup\n\n```python\nimport dspy\n\n# Define a basic module\nqa = dspy.ChainOfThought(\"question -> answer\")\n```\n\n## BestOfN Tutorial\n\n### Basic Usage\n\n```python\ndef one_word_answer(args, pred):\n    return 1.0 if len(pred.answer.split()) == 1 else 0.0\n\nbest_of_3 = dspy.BestOfN(\n    module=qa, \n    N=3, \n    reward_fn=one_word_answer, \n    threshold=1.0\n)\n\nresult = best_of_3(question=\"What is the capital of Belgium?\")\nprint(result.answer)\n```\n\n### Configuring Failure Tolerance\n\n```python\n# Allow only 1 failure out of 3 attempts\nstrict_best_of_3 = dspy.BestOfN(\n    module=qa, \n    N=3, \n    reward_fn=one_word_answer, \n    threshold=1.0,\n    fail_count=1\n)\n```\n\n### Use Case: Ensuring Factual Correctness\n\n```python\ndef factual_accuracy(args, pred):\n    # Implement your factual check\n    key_facts = extract_key_facts(args.question)\n    return calculate_coverage(pred.answer, key_facts)\n\ncorrectness_checker = dspy.BestOfN(\n    module=qa,\n    N=5,\n    reward_fn=factual_accuracy,\n    threshold=0.8,\n    fail_count=2\n)\n```\n\n## Refine Tutorial\n\n### Basic Usage\n\n```python\nrefine = dspy.Refine(\n    module=qa, \n    N=3, \n    reward_fn=one_word_answer, \n    threshold=1.0\n)\n\nresult = refine(question=\"What is the capital of Belgium?\")\nprint(result.answer)\n```\n\n### Configuring Failure Tolerance\n\n```python\n# Allow only 1 failure before raising an exception\nstrict_refine = dspy.Refine(\n    module=qa, \n    N=3, \n    reward_fn=one_word_answer, \n    threshold=1.0,\n    fail_count=1\n)\n```\n\n### Use Case: Control Response Length\n\n```python\ndef length_constraint(args, pred):\n    word_count = len(pred.answer.split())\n    return 1.0 if 50 <= word_count <= 100 else 0.0\n\nlength_refiner = dspy.Refine(\n    module=qa,\n    N=3,\n    reward_fn=length_constraint,\n    threshold=1.0\n)\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\nBoth modules support configurable failure tolerance through the `fail_count` parameter:\n\n- **Default** (`fail_count=N`): All N attempts must fail before raising\n- **Strict** (`fail_count=0`): First failure immediately raises\n- **Flexible** (`fail_count=N-1`): Up to N-1 failures tolerated\n\nError messages clearly indicate which attempt failed and at what temperature.\n\n## Complete Example: BestOfN\n\n```python\nimport dspy\n\nqa = dspy.ChainOfThought(\"question -> answer\")\n\ndef reward_fn(args, pred):\n    return 1.0 if len(pred.answer.split()) <= 5 else 0.0\n\nbest_of_5 = dspy.BestOfN(\n    module=qa,\n    N=5,\n    reward_fn=reward_fn,\n    threshold=1.0,\n    fail_count=2\n)\n\n# This will try up to 5 times, allowing 2 failures\nresult = best_of_5(question=\"What is machine learning?\")\nprint(result.answer)\n```\n\n## Complete Example: Refine\n\n```python\nimport dspy\n\nqa = dspy.ChainOfThought(\"question -> answer\")\n\ndef reward_fn(args, pred):\n    return 1.0 if len(pred.answer.split()) <= 5 else 0.0\n\nrefine = dspy.Refine(\n    module=qa,\n    N=5,\n    reward_fn=reward_fn,\n    threshold=1.0,\n    fail_count=2\n)\n\n# This will try up to 5 times with adaptive feedback\nresult = refine(question=\"What is machine learning?\")\nprint(result.answer)\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n1. **Choose appropriate N**: More attempts increase success likelihood but cost more\n2. **Set reasonable thresholds**: Too strict may cause all attempts to fail\n3. **Use fail_count wisely**: Higher values tolerate more failures but may mask bugs\n4. **Monitor error messages**: Temperature information helps debug issues\n\n## Migration from Older Approaches\n\nIf you're using older assertion-based retry logic:\n\n```python\n# Old approach\nfor i in range(N):\n    result = module(**kwargs)\n    if check_assertion(result):\n        break\n\n# New BestOfN approach\nbest_of_n = dspy.BestOfN(\n    module=module,\n    N=N,\n    reward_fn=lambda kwargs, pred: 1.0 if check_assertion(pred) else 0.0,\n    threshold=1.0\n)\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Explore [BestOfN API reference](../api/modules/BestOfN.md) for complete documentation\n- Check [Refine API reference](../api/modules/Refine.md) for advanced features\n- See practical use cases in the [DSPy use cases guide](../../dspy-usecases.md)\n","filePath":"/testbed/docs/docs/tutorials/output_refinement/index.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/testbed/docs/docs/tutorials/output_refinement/index.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"docs/docs/tutorials/output_refinement/index.md","time":{"start":1788420343939,"end":1788420343948}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_06628bf98001lH4ePK3b8zltO2","sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","messageID":"msg_06628b9d6001TT7KbpN0Dt83dZ"}}
