{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788420373445,"sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_25b57c4426f24efa883777a9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /testbed && python -c \"import inspect; from dspy.predict.best_of_n import BestOfN; print(inspect.getdoc(BestOfN.__init__))\""},"output":"Runs a module up to `N` times with different temperatures and returns the best prediction or the first prediction that passes the `threshold`.\n\nThis module runs the provided module multiple times with varying temperature settings and selects\neither the first prediction that exceeds the specified threshold or the one with the highest reward.\nIf no prediction meets the threshold, it automatically raises an exception based on the fail_count parameter.\n\nArgs:\n    module: The module to run.\n    N: The number of times to run the module.\n    reward_fn: The reward function.\n    threshold: The threshold for the reward function.\n    fail_count: The maximum number of failed attempts to tolerate. If not provided, defaults to N,\n                meaning all N attempts must fail before an exception is raised.\n\nExample:\n    >>> import dspy\n    >>> qa = dspy.ChainOfThought(\"question -> answer\")\n    >>> def one_word_answer(args, pred):\n    >>>     return 1.0 if len(pred.answer) == 1 else 0.0\n    >>> best_of_3 = dspy.BestOfN(module=qa, N=3, reward_fn=one_word_answer, threshold=1.0)\n    >>> best_of_3(question=\"What is the capital of Belgium?\").answer\n    >>> # Brussels\n","metadata":{"output":"Runs a module up to `N` times with different temperatures and returns the best prediction or the first prediction that passes the `threshold`.\n\nThis module runs the provided module multiple times with varying temperature settings and selects\neither the first prediction that exceeds the specified threshold or the one with the highest reward.\nIf no prediction meets the threshold, it automatically raises an exception based on the fail_count parameter.\n\nArgs:\n    module: The module to run.\n    N: The number of times to run the module.\n    reward_fn: The reward function.\n    threshold: The threshold for the reward function.\n    fail_count: The maximum number of failed attempts to tolerate. If not provided, defaults to N,\n                meaning all N attempts must fail before an exception is raised.\n\nExample:\n    >>> import dspy\n    >>> qa = dspy.ChainOfThought(\"question -> answer\")\n    >>> def one_word_answer(args, pred):\n    >>>     return 1.0 if len(pred.answer) == 1 else 0.0\n    >>> best_of_3 = dspy.BestOfN(module=qa, N=3, reward_fn=one_word_answer, threshold=1.0)\n    >>> best_of_3(question=\"What is the capital of Belgium?\").answer\n    >>> # Brussels\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /testbed && python -c \"import inspect; from dspy.predict.best_of_n import BestOfN; print(inspect.getdoc(BestOfN.__init__))\"","time":{"start":1788420371156,"end":1788420373442}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_0662932a30012NFpf5ZSPxgbqP","sessionID":"ses_f99d7a776ffe69blEyxQoKXLA0","messageID":"msg_0662930b1001myrFxWghZgo1E6"}}
